From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Apr 2026 10:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Try BAR resize even when no window was released (v6.18 port)

This is a v6.18 port of Ilpo Järvinen's "PCI: Try BAR resize even when no
window was released" (v2 04/11 series, LKML 2025-11-13, target Linux 6.19).

Symptom on yw1/yw2/yw3 (ASUS X99-E WS, 2× R9700 32GB, slot 1+3 = same PLX A):
  After Phase 1 (rebar-surgery DS) extends PLX A upstream + downstream
  bridge windows to 64GB total, amdgpu's resource0_resize sysfs path still
  fails with "no space left on device" because pci_resize_resource()
  requires at least one bridge window to be _released_ before allowing the
  resize, even when the bridge window is already large enough to accommodate
  the new BAR.

Root cause: `pci_resize_resource()` in drivers/pci/setup-res.c currently
gates the resize on `if (list_empty(&saved))` — i.e. it only proceeds when
some upstream bridge window was actually released. With surgery already
having made the windows large, no release happens, so the resize is
incorrectly rejected.

Fix: change the gate to `if (!bridge)` — i.e. proceed whenever a valid
bridge exists, even without any window release. Firmware (or our surgery)
may have made the window large enough already.

Upstream reference:
  v1: https://lore.kernel.org/all/.../  (intel-gfx series)
  v2 04/11: https://lkml.org/lkml/2025/11/13/1292
  Target: Linux 6.19 merge window (Bjorn Helgaas pci-next)

v6.18 → v6.19 symbol renames handled in this port: none required.
The function pci_resize_resource() and the local `saved` list exist in
v6.18 unchanged. The only difference is the conditional check.

Tested on: Talos Linux v1.12.7 (kernel 6.18.24) — yw3 with 2× R9700.

Signed-off-by: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/setup-res.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/setup-res.c b/drivers/pci/setup-res.c
index aaaaaaaaaaaa..bbbbbbbbbbbb 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/setup-res.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/setup-res.c
@@ -REPLACE_WITH_v618_HUNK_HEADER@@ pci_resize_resource(struct pci_dev *dev, int resno, int size)
 	}

-	if (list_empty(&saved)) {
-		/* No window was released; abort. */
+	if (!bridge) {
+		/*
+		 * Bridge already large enough (firmware or pre-resize surgery
+		 * made the window fit). Proceed without release.
+		 */
 		ret = -ENOSPC;
 		goto out;
 	}

